dossow1@jhuapl.edu (Bill Doss) writes:

> I feel I would be better served with an 1st level spell
> I could actually use than one I can't.  I love the ID spell, I just
> tend to YASD before I can learn to cast it well enough to use it.

Well, if you keep on dying before you can learn a 3rd level spell,
then having an extra 1st level spell will not really help you in the
end.

The 1st level spells are:
  - sleep
  - light
  - detect monsters
  - healing
  - knock
  - force bolt
  - protection
  - jumping

Only force bolt and healing are true life savers for early game
wizards. Sleep is useful in large rooms but very dangerous in confined
space and poor-skilled protection doesn't give enough AC for long
enoug time to be worthvile in my opinion. Detect monsters may reveal
you the odd fox but then you may not have enough spell points left to
kill it with a force bolt. 

But now, consider what spells would be lost for wizards if your
suggestion was implemented:
 
 - cause fear
 - charm monster
 - clairvoyance
 - confuse monster
 - create monster
 - cure blindness
 - cure sickness
 - detect food
 - detect unseen
 - drain life
 - extra healing
 - haste self
 - identify
 - magic missile
 - remove curse
 - slow monster
 - stone to flesh
 - wizard lock

This list contains the two by far most useful spells of the whole
game: magic missile and identify. Also, charm monster, extra healing,
remove curse, wizard lock, and slow monster are very good life savers
for early-game wizards. Create monster combined with an early altar
equals to Magicbane.

Restricting wizards spellbooks to first level would hurt much more
than help. 

